- decided_at: 2026-09-22T02:41:49+00:00
  event: initial
  value: Escape cancels the foreground agent turn or direct shell command, while explicitly backgrounded processes remain running; shell cancellation terminates the process tree with a direct-process fallback on Windows.
  reason: Foreground-only cancellation matches user intent without destroying persistent servers; process-tree termination prevents orphaned children, and the Windows fallback handles restricted taskkill environments.
- decided_at: 2026-09-27T00:24:52+00:00
  event: superseded-previous
  value: Escape cancels the foreground shell command first when it runs beside an agent turn, then the agent turn on the next press; explicitly backgrounded processes remain running; shell cancellation terminates the process tree with a direct-process fallback on Windows.
  reason: Shell-mode commands may now run while the agent works (one foreground shell at a time); cancelling the command the user started last matches intent, and cancelling both at once would kill a turn the user did not mean to stop.
- decided_at: 2026-10-07T04:48:39+00:00
  event: superseded-previous
  value: Escape cancels the foreground user shell first, then the agent run; at a tool approval Escape denies and cancels the run, whereas Enter/n deny only. Cancellation blocks subsequent retries, replies, tools and turns, rejects stale run events/approvals, and displays canceling until worker completion. Explicit background processes and session-lifetime child agents remain independent.
  reason: Keep the established shell-first behavior and Runner-owned child lifetime. Missing context checks and queued activity could revive canceled turns; stopping the UI alone would leave model/tool work running.
